%N A400331 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(8,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to 8. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400331 Closed under multiplication; see A400096 for details.
%H A400331 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400331/b400331.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..822</a> (all terms <= 10^10)
%e A400331 Powers of 7 are terms: 7^n -> 7^(n-1) -> ... -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400331 127 is a term: 127 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400331 337 is a term: 337 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400331 4432676798593 is a term: 4432676798593 -> 49 -> 7 -> 1;
%e A400331 2741672362528725535068727 is a term: 2741672362528725535068727 -> 49 -> 7 -> 1.
%t A400331 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400331 Select[Range[700000], okQ[#, 8] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
%o A400331 (PARI) isok(n, 8) \\ see A400096 for isok
